(Apply for the FSE Student Challenge Seed Fund 2026/2027) Tj
T*
T*
(Are you part of a student team gearing up to compete in an \(inter\)national student challenge?) Tj
T*
(The FSE Student Challenge Seed Fund is here to help you take your idea to the next level. Last) Tj
T*
(year we sponsored the Makercie team participating in the European Rover Challenge, the HARD) Tj
T*
(racing team going to France, and one team participating in the CanSat Mundial in Mexico.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(Who can apply) Tj
T*
(- Teams participating in the qualifications or finals of an \(inter\)national student competition) Tj
T*
(- Teams including BSc/MSc students from at least two different FSE programmes or from one FSE) Tj
T*
(programme together with students from Hanze University of Applied Sciences and/or MBO) Tj
T*
(Noorderpoort) Tj
T*
(- Each team can apply only once per competition round) Tj
T*
(- Applications are processed on a first come, first served basis. Please note that the) Tj
T*
(available budget is limited.) Tj
T*
(- There is limited room for bottom-up initiatives that do not fully meet these criteria but) Tj
T*
(align with the faculty's strengths and have a strong potential to generate publicity. Such) Tj
T*
(cases will be evaluated by a small committee) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(What's in it for you) Tj
T*
(- Seed funding covering up to EUR 5,000 for equipment, software, and hardware) Tj
T*
(- Three travel grants of up to EUR 1,000 each to help your team go global) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(When and how to apply) Tj
T*
(Your application should include:) Tj
T*
(- A short description of the competition, with relevant website links) Tj
T*
(- An itemised cost breakdown) Tj
T*
(- The name\(s\) of the professors or expert-faculty staff supporting the team) Tj
T*
(- A timeline describing the planned activities, including qualification rounds and finals, with) Tj
T*
(dates and locations) Tj
T*
(- A short plan on how additional funding and support will be acquired, and which types of) Tj
T*
(support and equipment are needed) Tj
T*
(- A list of team members, including their study programme at FSE, Hanze, or MBO, their student) Tj
T*
(numbers, and their roles and responsibilities within the team) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(This can be submitted to Prof. Marc van der Maarel, FSE Student Challenge Coordinator) Tj
T*
(\(m.j.e.c.van.der.maarel@rug.nl\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(Deadlines: November 15 2026 or March 1 2027) Tj
T*
(Applications are processed on a first come, first served basis. Please note that the available) Tj
T*
(budget is limited.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(Important) Tj
T*
(To be eligible to receive the fund, a team that is not an officially registered foundation) Tj
T*
(\(stichting\) or association \(vereniging\) must either be, or become, a committee of the GEARS) Tj
T*
(study association. In addition, all members of the team must be, or become, members of GEARS.) Tj
T*
(Funding will be transferred to GEARS, which will support the team in administering and spending) Tj
T*
(the funds in accordance with the approved project budget. Newly established foundations created) Tj
T*
(solely for the purpose of receiving the FSE Student Challenge Seed Fund are not eligible. The) Tj
T*
(FSE Student Challenge Seed Fund does not cover the costs associated with establishing a) Tj
